# Where the backend lives.
#
# Leave EMPTY in development. The client then uses "/api", which vite proxies to
# localhost:4100 — the browser sees one origin, so CORS never applies locally.
#
# In production set this to the deployed backend's ORIGIN, e.g.
# "https://api.example.com". Requests then become cross-origin, which is the
# point at which enableCors() on the backend must be narrowed to this app's
# origin (it currently allows everything).
VITE_API_URL=""
